    "created_at": "2023-04-14T22:33:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-14T22:33:01Z",
    "body": "So we discussed other such \"interactions\" between things that can be in the top layer in multiple ways, here: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9045\r\n\r\nThe general conclusion/direction seems to be that these things should only be allowed to be in the top layer in one of the ways at a time. So `a.showPopover(); a.requestFullscreen()` should reject the fullscreen request because the element is already a showing popover. But `a.showPopover();a.hidePopover();a.requestFullscreen()` should be ok. I.e. both are allowed, just one at a time.\r\n\r\n@josepharhar has a PR against fullscreen, I think, to do the above. Is that right?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/fullscreen/issues/comments/1509360797/reactions",
